 that she has learned to love the  chaos the noise and the hugs and the  other parts of parenthood - the chores  are apparently split between all the  members of the household above the age  of 8 years old the craziest detail of  this family dynamic is perhaps the fact  that bonell drives all of her kids to  school in a 16 cedar mercedes school bus  the launce family the launce family is  made up of 18 mmm  they live in British Columbia Canada but  originally immigrated from Romania in  1990 their last reported child was born  in 2008 the reasoning behind their  decision to start their uniquely large  family seems to be a spiritual one they  mentioned that they decided to leave the  decision of how many children they were  to have up to God this has left them  with eight boys and ten girls to date  despite being offered a ton of lucrative  TV series and documentary contracts the  family has continuously rejected these  offers  they have only appeared in a handful of  interviews and choose to live a more  private and low-key life the Bates  family Gil and Kelly Bates are two  parents who have chosen to embrace the  cameras and not shy away from life on  television the Bates starred on their  very own TV series on up TV this series  featured both parents and their 19  children the family lives in a six  bedroom house which consists of one  guest room and five others for the  personal use of the family with the  parents taking a room to themselves this  leaves just two rooms for the boys and  two rooms for the girls we sure hope  they all get along or that could be a  pretty sticky situation we bet the Louds  are feeling pretty good about themselves  right now the Bell Salak family we've  decided to take it up a notch and bring  you guys a family with no less than 59  children the story behind this family  which makes up 61 members if you factor  in the parents is actually very sweet  and inspiring the father of the family  Jim Silla met his wife and bells and  married her after just four months since  then the couple went on to adopt 59 kids  all of whom are boys not only that but  all of these children knowingly have  some sort of disability which did not  deter the couple in the slightest their  home is equipped with a team of nurses  teachers and aides  all of whom consistently ensure that  everything is running smoothly and that  everyone is being taken care of and  bells even as a keepsake box for each of  the boys the boxes are said to have  pictures and art need by the boys along  with some mementos that they arrived  with she mentions that this is her and  her husband's attempt to piece back the  children's history if that isn't the  sweetest story you've heard all day we  don't know what is the chiana family the  channa family is the largest family on  our list and they live in the village in  India their family consists  39 wives 14 daughters-in-law ninety four  children and 33 grandchildren this leads  to a total of 180 family members they  catch in this family stories that they  all live in one giant four-story mansion  which has a hundred rooms to accommodate  the little village of the family members  this house actually has a name and is  known by the villagers as the house of  the new generation there was once a  documentary made of the family where you  can even spot the family taking turns  doing chores with a large number of them  dedicated to laundry cooking and singing  the family gets along very well and are  very happy to be living under one roof  in the documentary you can spot some of  the children proudly showing the  videographers around the house that they  share many of the women even mentioned  how happy they are to be with their  large and loving family since it's a lot  more interesting than their old and  simple lives the family sustains itself  by growing their very own props and even  establishing their very own school the  family even wakes up and goes to bed  together starting their days at 5: